{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>ולא יעבור עליו לכל דבר</b> — a matter of the army: for any matter that is a need of the army, whether to supply water and food or to repair roads. But those who return from the ranks of the battle line by the word of the priest — such as one who built a new house and has not dedicated it, or betrothed a woman and has not taken her — they do supply water and food and repair the roads. This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Deuteronomy 24:5), from the words of our Sages (Sifrei 137; Sotah 44a). If so, then <b>עליו</b> refers to the army mentioned: it says that this man shall not pass over the army for any matter — not to be an officer over the men of the army, or to muster the people of the land, or for anything they need such as supplying water; he shall have no responsibility over them but only for his rejoicing. And this is the correct interpretation."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:54:46.988309655Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}